# Warren update-channel Ed25519 metadata signing public keys.
#
# Each non-comment, non-empty line is a single 64-character hex-encoded
# Ed25519 verifying key. Comments start with `#`. Trailing whitespace is
# stripped per `parse_keys` in `src/defaults.rs`.
#
# This key can ship an installer to every user, so it is the highest-
# privilege key in the system. It signs the software we ship and nothing
# else (these app update manifests, and the SHA256SUMS of every warren-cli
# release through ci/sign-headless-sums.sh). Do NOT reuse the relay/admin
# signing key (its lineage was burned once:
# `admin/admin-signing.key.BURNED-committed-do-not-use`).
#
# The matching Ed25519 secret is kept offline by poka and is also the CI
# secret `WARREN_UPDATE_SIGNING_KEY`, so it is an online key: only the
# signing job of `.github/workflows/update-metadata.yml` reads it, in one
# step, on a fresh GitHub-hosted VM in the `update-signing` environment, with
# no compilation and no third-party action. A `warren-vpn` daemon shipped with this
# trust file accepts manifests signed by the key below and rejects all
# others (fail-closed).
#
# Key rotation: add the new pubkey on its own line (both are then trusted
# during the overlap), ship a release, then drop the retired line. The
# warren-cli installers pin this key too; move their pins before the first
# CLI release signed by a new key.
